# IDEA Template — Universal capture artifact for the Rhumb Workflow Protocol
#
# DESIGN PROVENANCE
# This template inherits from AVD-0009 KD-09-02 (Open/Closed Split Table OPEN
# row: Artifacts + Schemas + State Machines ship under Apache 2.0) and from
# ACS-0038 KD-38.1..7. KD-38.3 strips runtime and commercial-tier fields
# (cost-tracking metadata, internal pipeline variants, runtime metadata
# pointers); KD-38.5 sets the pipeline enum to {direct, architecture,
# one_off}; KD-38.7 declines to standardize parked/roadmap/backlog
# directory layout (advisory only).
#
# PRECEDENCE RULE (KD-38.2 — frontmatter wins on conflict)
# When `status:` (frontmatter) and file location disagree (e.g.,
# status=approved but file in ideas/captured/), tooling MUST trust
# frontmatter. Lifecycle-by-location stays advisory for human navigation;
# rhumb-validate Level-3 gating consumes frontmatter only.
#
# UNIVERSAL CAPTURE
# IDEA is the universal capture artifact in the Rhumb Workflow Protocol.
# Every thought, feature request, bug report, architectural concept, or
# strategic initiative starts as an IDEA. What happens after capture
# depends on the 7-state lifecycle and the `pipeline:` routing field
# (decided at `approved` time).
#
# ─── Lifecycle (7-state enum) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#   captured  → just dropped in; no refinement cycle yet
#   refining  → refinement in motion (brainstorming, shaping)
#   ready     → refinement done; awaiting human approval
#   approved  → human said yes; awaiting promotion
#   promoted  → promoted_to is set (downstream artifact assigned)
#   parked    → deferred (uses parked_as: any string label)
#   discarded → killed (with discarded_reason)
#
# ─── Lifecycle-by-location (advisory only) ────────────────────────────
# Implementations MAY organize IDEAs by directory (e.g., ideas/captured/,
# ideas/promoted/) for human navigation, but MUST NOT use directory
# location as the source of truth for `status`. Per KD-38.7, directory
# layout — including any roadmap/backlog folders for parked items — is
# implementation-specific and NOT normative.
#
# ─── Pipeline routing (set at `approved` time) ────────────────────────
#   architecture → IDEA → AVD(s) → ACS(es) → MP(s) → Execution (rigor path)
#   direct       → IDEA → MP → Execution (fast path; directly plannable work)
#   one_off      → IDEA → direct execution, no MP (single-shot work)
#
# Path selection is methodology, not runtime. Implementations MUST surface
# `pipeline` in IDEA frontmatter; tooling MUST validate the value against
# the {direct, architecture, one_off} enum. Default-to-architecture-when-
# ambiguous is the recommended posture (see prose spec).
#
# IDEAs are intentionally lightweight at creation. No required body sections
# beyond the frontmatter — capture the thought, refine later. Architecture-
# pipeline IDEAs typically grow Resolved Decisions, Present State Audit,
# and Path Selection sections before AVD promotion.

id: IDEA-NNNN
type: idea
title: "[IDEA Title]"
status: captured                      # captured | refining | ready | approved | promoted | parked | discarded
classification: public                # public | confidential
created: {{TIMESTAMP}}
updated: {{TIMESTAMP}}

# Authors — supports human + AI collaboration; minimum one entry
authors:
  - name: "[Author name]"
    role: "[architect | engineer | pm | assistant | reviewer | other]"
tags: []                              # Optional; domain tags for indexing

# ─── Chain linkage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
parent: null                          # Upstream artifact: IDEA-NNNN | REQ-NNNNN | null
children: []                          # Downstream artifacts: AVD-NNNN, MP-NNNN, etc.

# ─── Pipeline routing (decided at `approved` time) ────────────────────────
pipeline: null                        # direct | architecture | one_off | null
                                      # null         = not yet routed
                                      # architecture = IDEA → AVD(s) → ACS(es) → MP(s) (rigor path)
                                      # direct       = IDEA → MP (fast path; directly plannable)
                                      # one_off      = direct execution, no MP (single-shot)

# ─── Lifecycle metadata (sparse — populated as states are reached) ────────
# All fields below are optional in JSON Schema; per-state required fields
# are enforced separately by the lifecycle spec + validator (KD-38.6).

# Approval (status: approved)
approved_by: null                     # Plain string (name or handle)
approved_at: null                     # ISO-8601
approval_policy: null                 # e.g. "solo" | "review" | implementation-specific

# Promotion (status: promoted)
promoted_to: null                     # AVD-NNNN | MP-NNNN | downstream artifact ID
promoted_at: null                     # ISO-8601
promoted_pipeline: null               # direct | architecture | one_off

# Parking (status: parked)
parked_as: null                       # Free string label (e.g., "roadmap", "backlog", impl-specific)
parked_reason: null                   # Why deferred
parked_until: null                    # ISO-8601 | null (open-ended)

# Discarding (status: discarded)
discarded_by: null                    # Plain string
discarded_at: null                    # ISO-8601
discarded_reason: null                # Why killed (REQUIRED when status=discarded)
---

